jarvisagent (0.8.6) noble; urgency=medium

  * Repository layout reorganised: all source now lives under code/
    (backend, frontend, mcp, vendor); the project root is minimal.
  * Source packages are assembled with `git archive` (version-controlled
    files only) so local secrets and runtime data are never included.
  * queue/ and workflows/ folders are created automatically on first start.
  * AI-interface connectivity probe timeout raised to 90s so local LLM
    endpoints (Ollama / vLLM) cold-loading large models register as online.

 -- JC <beaumanvienna@gmail.com>  Thu, 04 Jun 2026 04:50:55 +0000

jarvisagent (0.8.5) noble; urgency=medium

  * Dual-edition build: --engine flag produces jarvisAgent-engine,
    default produces jarvisAgent-studio (no manual copy step)
  * Separate objdirs per edition (bin-int/engine/ vs bin-int/studio/)
  * Edition contract tests (test/test_edition_contract.py)
  * All 10 packaging targets updated for new binary naming
  * Frontend capability-gating via /api/status edition + capabilities

 -- JC <beaumanvienna@gmail.com>  Tue, 01 Apr 2026 20:00:00 +0000

jarvisagent (0.8.2) noble; urgency=medium

  * Use shared jarvisagent-launcher.sh instead of old jarvisagent.wrapper
  * Python venv created in user-space ~/JarvisAgent/.venv on first launch
    (no longer installed system-wide in postinst)
  * postinst/postrm aligned with RPM, Arch, and local DEB packaging

